{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch49rCVgDz21JGASRUQro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `scripts/export_invoices.py`, ran it, and committed the script and the output together as `718affc`. It wrote 9 rows to `out/invoices.csv`, with no segment C rows.\n\n**Segment C is left out of this export too.** The customers export drops segment C, and the commit that added that rule (`1db5abc`) explains why. Those customers declined partner sharing, and the contract covers *every record* held on them, not just the customers table. Each invoice row has a `seg` column, so the script drops `seg == C` rows the same way. Otherwise their invoices would go to the partner. My commit message points back to `1db5abc`.\n\nThe script is a copy of `export_customers.py` with only the table names changed. I didn't run `check.sh` because it only applies to files under `data/`. January is untouched: the copy is out of `data/` and the original is still in `inbox/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":18129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":406},"output_tokens":286,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-46>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T05:22:14.072Z","request_id":"req_011Ch49rCJWj2rbnt3vLZTFj"}
